WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.534
-Wow, wow.
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.234
I am so happy you're here.
You look sharp, as always.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.701
-Thank you. Likewise.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:08.834
-You know, I am such a big fan
of your work for a long time.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.300
I've known you,
and I've always run into you.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.133
You're always a nice guy to me
and everything.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.033
And I got to say, you did this

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:18.033
"Searching for Italy:
Stanley Tucci" on CNN.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.567
I loved it so much.
I freaked out.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.634
I -- It's -- I want to get into
all of the details.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.868
But I loved everything.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.200
I loved the episode
with the hailstorm.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.534
-Oh, yeah.
-When everyone was locked in.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.767
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah.
-But then I felt inspired.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.934
I felt like I became,
like, inspired.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.601
I should be a chef.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.200
-And I felt like, "If Stanley
is telling me what to do..."

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.000
I thought through the TV,
you're talking to me

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.434
and saying, "Jimmy, go out
and make a pizza yourself."

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.801
-Yes, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.834
-"Don't just microwave a pizza.
Go make it yourself."

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.300
-Yes, do it yourself.
-So I did it.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.567
And I did it -- I made it.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.968
I was inspired.
I put it on -- on YouTube.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.234
-Yes.
-Because I was inspired.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.667
I wanted to show
other people how --

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.067
that I know how to do it.
-Yes.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:55.767
-And, of course, Jimmy Kimmel,

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.968
who really knows
a lot about pizza...

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.901
-Yes.
-...just destroyed my video.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:04.067
-Yeah. Yeah.
He's -- he's tough. He's tough.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.300
-He -- No, he really knows
his pizza, by the way.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.234
And he was just like --
He e-mailed me before he did it.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.367
He goes, "Dude, what?
I got to respond to this thing.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.868
This is insane."

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.734
And I go -- 'Cause I was like --
I was rolling it.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:14.934
-Yeah.
-With a roller.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.634
And he said,
"Don't ever do that."

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:17.801
-No.
-No, no, I didn't know.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.234
-No -- Yeah.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.767
-Yeah, it was just every single
mistake I could ever make.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.601
-But he's --
But he's sort of beyond --

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:24.701
He's not -- I mean --
-He's not normal, is he?

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.067
-I've eaten pizza at his house.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.067
-No, he's --
-And it's -- it's incredible.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.767
-No, he takes it
to the next level.

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:32.000
-No, and I can't
make pizza like that.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
No, he's -- I'm not kidding.
He really is amazing.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.200
-I think you inadvertently
restarted the late-night wars.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.267
That's just it.
Just by that pizza thing.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.701
-Yeah, yeah.
-But I -- I saw this --

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.033
-I felt there
was something lacking.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.367
-Yeah, thank you.
You're always --

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.167
You're always spicing up life.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.667
-I love that.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.934
-But you've inspired people
to -- to travel and to cook.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.267
It's a big deal.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.734
In Italy,
I've read these articles

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.934
where people are having
Stanley Tucci tours.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.234
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.234
-That must feel good, right?
-Yeah, it feels great.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.467
I mean, I'd love a piece
of the action, but, you know...

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.334
-No, no, no.
Yeah, you can't do that.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:10.667
-No, no, I can't do that.
No, but it's wonderful.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.901
It -- Well, you know, look, when
the show came out, we were --

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.067
You know, it was during,
you know, the pandemic.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.767
-Sure. Of course.
-During lockdown.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.968
So we had a captive audience,
right?

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.234
And people were desperate
to get out.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:25.834
And they sort of
lived vicariously through us.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.634
-You won two Emmys for it.
-Yes.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.334
-For "Searching for Italy."
Two Emmys.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.334
-Yes, yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:32.834
Yes.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.734
-Well-deserved.
-Thank you.

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.167
Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.567
-Will there be a season three?
-Yes, I hope there will be.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.434
Unfortunately, CNN has canceled

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.367
all of their
original programming,

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:47.334
so hopefully we'll end up
on another streamer, network.

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.868
We don't know.
-Wow.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.868
-But, yes, I have plans to do
season three and more.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.667
-So, "Searching for Italy"
is searching for a new network.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.801
-Searching --
Searching for a network.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:58.968
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.033
Not as appetizing.
-No, no.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.567
[ Laughter ]
I just love that you did that.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.133
And then I love that.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:08.100
And then you also posted
something on Instagram.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.601
-Yeah.
-Of you making a cocktail.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:14.167
A Negroni.
And it went viral beyond belief.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.868
-Yes, I know.
-You -- Yeah, and I was like,

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.300
"This is -- This is everything.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.968
Stanley Tucci is owning
the world right now."

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.734
We loved it. It was so good.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.334
I mean, did you know that
you were going to go that --

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.167
-No, no.
-You're just making it for fun?

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.968
-No, I did it --
I did it because --

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:32.434
I did it for my agency
in England, Curtis Brown.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.000
My wife works there.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.100
-And she said, "Make a cocktail
for everybody during lockdown.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.167
It'd be really nice.

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.601
And, you know, people --
cheer them up."

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.868
-Yeah.
-So I did that.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.701
And then she said, "Well,
put it on your Instagram."

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:43.734
And then she showed me
how to do that.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.834
[ Laughter ]
And then I did it.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:47.767
-Yeah.
-And then that happened.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.167
-Yeah.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.133
-And then Chris Evans tweeted
it or re-something'ed it.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.300
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.868
-And then it went
completely crazy.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.801
-Yeah, Chris Evans.
That's right. He loved it.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:58.367
-Chris Evans.
Anything he touches. Yeah.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.934
-Turns to gold, yeah.
-It's true, yeah.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.534
-But the big hot drink now
is Negroni sbagliatos.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:04.667
-Sbagliato, yes.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.100
-Sbagliato.
With prosecco in it.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.634
-It's all over TikTok.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.901
-And I don't -- I just --
I have two made here tonight.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.334
-Oh, wow. What do you know?

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.868
-I did not make these.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:17.667
I thought maybe we could
have a taste test.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.067
'Cause when you do a Negroni,
just -- you do a normal Negroni.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.367
Is that correct?
-I do, I do.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.968
But I -- I like mine up,

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.767
as opposed to on the rocks,
the Negroni.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:26.868
But you wouldn't necessarily
do that with this.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:28.367
-Okay, okay.
-Yeah.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.601
-Cheers. Let's try this
and see how it tastes.

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:33.868
Me and Stanley Tucci
trying a Negroni sbagliato

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:35.901
with prosecco in it.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:38.234
[ Jazz music plays ]

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:42.234
♪♪

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:44.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.968
-I'd buy that for a dollar.
-Yeah.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.267
-Yeah, that's --
-That's pretty tasty.

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:51.400
-That's nice. It wants --

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.868
-It tastes a little
champagne-y to me.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.567
-It's a little too champagne-y.
-Prosecco-y. Yeah.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.033
-Prosecco-y, yeah.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:05:00.067
It should have a little more
of the harder alcohols in it.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.434
-Right?
-Yeah, I think so.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.734
-I agree. I think, yeah.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.534
-It really just needs,
like, a little --

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.067
It needs to be graced with it.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.701
-Yeah.
I think cheers, but this is --

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.634
I'm going to go with original
Stanley Tucci Negroni.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.133
Yeah, if you're going to go --

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:13.033
Yeah.
That's what I would go with.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.167
This came out. This went viral.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.267
And then
here you go on the list.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:20.434
You're one of the sexiest
bald men on the planet.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.067
And --
-Yeah.

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:25.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.701
-There you go. Number two.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.601
I don't know if you could --

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.801
I'm underneath --
-Barely, barely.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:34.167
-Barely.
-Barely.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.667
-6.3. Yeah.
-Barely there, yeah.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.100
But, hey,
there's always next year, bud.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.000
-Right.
There's always next year. Yes.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.334
-You're just crushing it
right now.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:42.734
-Yeah, oh, thank you.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.767
-I want to talk to you about
the Whitney Houston movie.

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.567
-Yeah.
-Gosh, it's beautiful.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.934
It's heartbreaking.

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.868
But you play
a legendary producer.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.434
-Yeah.
-Record legend Clive Davis

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:54.267
who discovered Whitney Houston.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.033
-Who is an actual
living real person.

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.567
-Yes, still.
-Is it hard to play someone

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.734
who is actually next to you
and go like,

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.834
"Well, that's really --
This is how I would do it"?

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:06.000
-No. Luckily, he wasn't on
the set when I was filming.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.133
-Good, good, good.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.567
-That would've been
disconcerting.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:12.033
He was -- I talked to him.
I saw the documentary about him.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.167
I read his book.
And then we had a Zoom call.

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:15.367
I was filming in Turin.

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:18.033
I was doing the episode
of Piemonte.

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:21.601
And he -- we talked for an hour,
and he was amazing.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:24.100
And then I met him for,
like, a half-hour before --

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.868
like, two days
before I started filming.

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:28.601
And he was nothing
but generous and kind.

00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:30.734
And he's fascinating.

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:33.601
We listened to --
The music we listen to today,

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:35.467
one of the reasons
is because of him.

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:36.801
-Yes.
-It's amazing.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:39.033
And this is a guy
who was a lawyer

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:41.968
and ended up in this job
sort of by happenstance.

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:43.133
-Yeah.

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.701
-And as it turns out,
he's not a singer.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:46.100
He's not a musician.
He's not a --

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.367
It turns out he just has
this incredible ear...

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:49.400
-Yeah.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.300
-...that now has informed
all of our ears.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.667
-Yeah, you're right.
-Yeah.

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.334
-And who's playing
Whitney Houston again?

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:56.000
-Naomi Ackie.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.934
This woman is -- This is
an extraordinary actress.

00:06:58.934 --> 00:07:01.033
-Naomi Ackie. It's unbelievable.
I want to show a clip.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.501
Here's Stanley Tucci in

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.000
"Whitney Houston:
I Wanna Dance with Somebody."

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.434
Take a look at this.

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:12.767
♪♪

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:16.901
-♪ How will I know
if he's thinking of me? ♪

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:19.133
♪ I try to phone,
but I'm too shy ♪

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:21.767
-Maybe.
-Maybe? Why?

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:23.434
-♪ Falling in love
is so bittersweet ♪

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:27.367
♪ How will I know
if he really loves me? ♪

00:07:27.367 --> 00:07:31.567
♪ I say a prayer
with every heartbeat ♪

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:33.634
You know?

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.367
I could do something
with the chorus.

00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:36.868
Go up a key there,
get more out of it.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:39.901
-Yeah, but that's not
a reason to -- to do a song.

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:41.634
It's gotta have a hook.

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:43.834
-A hook?
-Yeah.

00:07:43.834 --> 00:07:45.300
-I'll give it a hook.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.300
-Yeah. "I'll give it a hook."

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.400
Stanley Tucci, everybody.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.767
We love you, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:54.767
-"Whitney Houston:
I Wanna Dance with Somebody"

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:56.400
is in theaters December 23rd.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.033
We'll be right back with
Michael Che and Sean Patton.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:00.300
Stick around.

